(Three hundred seventy-six adults with plaque-type psoriasis were randomized to receive one) Tj
T*
(of four formulations: combination vitamin D analog and corticosteroid in either aerosol) Tj
T*
(foam or ointment vehicle, or respective vehicles alone. Primary efficacy endpoint defined) Tj
T*
(treatment success as physician-assessed clinical clearing or near-clearing with minimum) Tj
T*
(two-level improvement, assessed at week 4. The aerosol foam formulation achieved treatment) Tj
T*
(success in 55.3% of participants versus 42.8% receiving ointment \(p = 0.022\). Modified) Tj
T*
(disease area and severity index scores demonstrated significant between-group differences) Tj
T*
(favoring foam \(mean difference -0.62 points, p = 0.004\). Both active formulations produced) Tj
T*
(rapid and sustained itch improvement, with no meaningful differences between delivery) Tj
T*
(systems. Adverse events were minimal and comparable between groups; single case of mild) Tj
T*
(application site irritation with foam. These results demonstrate enhanced therapeutic) Tj
T*
(efficiency with foam-based delivery of topical combination therapy for psoriasis.) Tj
